From: "Baptiste G." <70719480+BeeeFX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:51:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Node graph: Viewer nodes, input labels, backdrops and
 badges optionally drawn like Nuke's

Preferences in Appearance > Node Graph > Node and link drawing, each off by default (Natron's drawing as before):
- linkLabelNearInput: a link's input label (A, B, Mask) sits beside the link close to the node it feeds, and a
  node's only input that isn't a mask has no label (connected or not), instead of every label mid-link.
- viewerNodePointed: Viewer nodes are drawn with pointed left and right ends (their outline too), so they stand out
  from the nodes that process images. Through a QGraphicsItem data key on the node's box (NodeGraphRectItem.h).
- backdropLabelOnly: a backdrop shows no name strip (the strip stays, unseen, to drag the backdrop by), only its
  label, twice the interface size unless the label chose its own size, at its top left.
- nodeBadgesFlat: the marks on a node's corners (E, P, V, C) are flat discs with a thin dark edge, not shaded.
- nodeNameKeepsSize: a node whose label has no text of its own draws its name like every other node's. Once a
  node's panel has been opened, Natron's label editor leaves an empty font tag (HTML size 6) in the label, which
  drew that node's name much larger than the others'.
- Every new preference is read by name, so Settings.h doesn't change.

Since the audit of 11 November 2026 (NAT-15): isOnlyMainInput tests the node's effect; a backdrop's label
has its own size only when a font tag gives one.

Core patch 0005 of the BeeeFX fork (layer/patches/), on top of 0001 and 0003, written to be offered upstream as it is.

Gap: layer/GAPS.md, "Nuke's look and habits" (the node graph's drawing: Viewer node, input labels, backdrops,
node badges).
Size: 6 files, 144 lines added, 9 removed.
upstream: not offered yet (the repository is public since 2 November 2026; offered once the two
fixes are in, Baptiste's call).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
